m early december on this  and certainly the indications we were  getting was that police officers who are  up close and personal with people we  can't police  um with social distance uh unfortunately  and many colleagues been spat out and  coughed out so there is a  i believe a very strong rationale as to  why my colleagues should be prioritized  there was an indication that they would  be  and that was snatched away and i think  some elements of the public sector we've  heard earlier  about teachers do feel bitterly let down  by this and i know it's a contentious  issue but if  my colleagues are expected to police in  the way that they're expected to police  they need to have the full support of  government and that also includes  having access to the vaccines we have a  hundred and thirty thousand police  officers  across england and wales nationally  including police staff and special  constables who are just  as deserving of this vaccine probably a  couple of hundred thousand  police officers and police staff that  would take probably half a day in the  current climate to vaccinate  um john public sectors  so sorry john we are once again out of  time but i'm sure it won't be too long  before we speak again john actor from  the police federation thanks very much  indeed  uh time for us uh to have the weather  here's isabelle  look forward to brighter skies the  weather  sponsored by qatar airways  brightening skies for the north and west  today quite pleasant actually with some  sunshine temperatures after a chilly  start getting up to about 12 in dublin  channel 11 for edinburgh now across  england and wells there is some rain  creeping its way gradually eastwards it  does cover central parts for a good part  of the day but then tending to tail off  by the time it gets into the southeast  not too bad tonight  but it's set to turn wet and windy  tomorrow  the weather sponsored by qatar airways
 

